"Which of the following quadratic forms over $R^{2}$ are negative semi-definite?\n\n1. $x^{T}Qx$, where the eigenvalues of $Q$ are $λ_{1} = 3$ and $λ_{2} = 5$\n2. $x^{T}Rx$, where the eigenvalues of $R$ are $λ_{1} = λ_{2} =-3$\n3. $x^{T}Sx$, where the eigenvalues of $S$ are $λ_{1} = 0$ and $λ_{2} =-1$"]]}]